# Restart AMBEserver when the vocoder dongle appears (docs/ZELLO.md).
#
# **AMBEserver survives losing its dongle, and that is the problem.** Unplug
# the dongle, or move it to another port, and the process keeps running: it
# holds a file descriptor for a device that no longer exists, keeps 2460 bound,
# accepts QSP's datagrams and never answers. systemctl still reports it active.
# QSP reports failing and warns on every call, but nothing recovers. Observed
# on production 2026-09-16 to 09-19: three days, 21 minutes of CPU burnt, 34 kB
# queued on the socket, and Zello silent both ways until AMBEserver was
# restarted by hand.
#
# **The rule only signals; it does not act.** systemctl in a udev RUN+= is
# discouraged upstream and can hang a udev worker until it is killed, so the
# work is in ambeserver-replug.service and this rule just asks for it. The
# device needs TAG+="systemd" for a .device unit to exist to hang that Wants on.
#
# Any FTDI serial adapter matches, not this dongle alone: narrowing it by serial
# number would mean every operator editing the file, and a needless AMBEserver
# restart is cheaper than a rule nobody adapts. It costs the call in progress.
ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="usb-serial", DRIVER=="ftdi_sio", \
  TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ambeserver-replug.service"
